  "name": "Voron 0.2 R1 Mini Stealthburner (official V0.2R1 master assembly, Revo Voron hotend)",
  "provenance": "Voron 0.2 R1 Mini Stealthburner (official V0.2R1 master assembly, Revo Voron hotend) Confidence: high. Sources: https://github.com/VoronDesign/Voron-0/blob/Voron0.2r1/CAD/V0.2R1_Master_Assembly_STEP.zip. Tip = lowest point of the Revo Voron solid in the official V0.2R1 master assembly STEP; axis = PTFE tube axis (x 0, y -24.56 in assembly). Assembly is Z-up, +Y rear, +X right already. Lowest non-nozzle part: Mini Stealthburner front cowling duct lips at z 1.80 mm, two lips at x +/-14.2..22.6, y -19.1..12.6 (lips rise outward: 25.9 wide at z 3.3, 27.4 at 5.8). Revo heater core starts at z 2.38 (r 5.5-6.5). Hotend choice in the Mini SB (Revo/Dragon/V6 mounts) does not move the cowling relative to the tip by design; non-Revo hotends were not separately measured. ADXL mount included (it sits at z>=59.6). Belts and the X-gantry extrusion/rail are reported as gantry, not as head parts. Boxes are mesh-section AABBs split per component and per XY-connected cluster; no margin applied. Nozzle: land radius 0.58 mm, 39.0-degree cone to Z=2.38, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 33.05 mm above the tip, Y 19.9..34.9, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/voron-mini-stealthburner.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
